Recent work investigates how the demographic and geo-cultural backgrounds of human raters fundamentally shape their perception of harm and safety in generative AI outputs. By developing new multimodal datasets and evaluation metrics, this research addresses the critical "blind spots" in current text-to-image and large language models, which often fail to account for diverse human values. The overarching goal of these current directions is to move beyond monolithic safety standards, ensuring that AI systems are aligned equitably across different global and cultural contexts.

